WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.716 --> 00:00:09.190
This page helps you read each assessment, see the course ideas it needs, and plan your start so the blank page never wins.

2
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:20.195
Walk the five assessments in order. From the Personal Cartography sequence and the Two-Eyed Seeing Journal to the final integration, each item names what kind of work it is and how the weekly rooms feed it.

3
00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:31.202
Keep the journal grounded. Two-Eyed Seeing Journal entries always work from the named source, in respectful, attributed language. That standard holds on every route.

4
00:00:31.202 --> 00:00:42.206
Read the dates and the integrity notes. Due dates cluster; see them early. And if an academic-integrity concern ever arises, the instructor contacts you first and you get the chance to explain your process.

5
00:00:42.207 --> 00:00:53.210
Open the Assignment Start Lab when you are stuck. Add your assignment, progress, exact sticking point, and available time. Fixed course rules build a personal start plan, without AI. You can print it or save it as a PDF.

6
00:00:53.210 --> 00:01:02.547
Submit on Blackboard, always. This site helps you plan. The official instructions, rubric, submission, and grade all live on Blackboard.

7
00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:07.590
Nothing here is graded. Blackboard is the only submission channel.

8
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.479
Where next: Block one hour, open the lab, and leave with a plan.
